A mischievous court jester in Renaissance attire crouches behind an ornate wooden desk, carefully placing a whoopee cushion on an elaborate throne, rendered in Leonardo da Vinci's style with soft sfumato technique, warm sepia tones, and delicate cross-hatching. The scene is set in a grand medieval study with arched windows casting diffused golden light, anatomical sketches and mechanical drawings visible on parchment scrolls in the background. The jester's expression captures gleeful anticipation, one finger pressed to smirking lips in a secretive gesture. Subtle details include a calendar on the wall showing the first day of the month, and scattered quill pens and ink pots on the desk. The composition uses da Vinci's signature atmospheric perspective, with the background fading into hazy blues and the foreground rendered in rich amber and burgundy tones.
